    docs: reconcile declared-table REST status
    
    README.md's roadmap section listed generic REST over declared tables
    (SUPA-3 / SUPA-6) as Planned while the shipped CLI/HTTP layer is
    documented later in the same file. Per the positioning policy a
    capability stays below "available now" until release evidence exists,
    so the roadmap statement, the declared-tables note, and the
    docs/guide/positioning.md capability matrix now all name the same
    status: "Implemented on branch — release evidence pending", citing the
    route mounts and named tests as evidence without claiming "Available
    now". positioning.md was changed because the README designates it as
    the owner of the four-status matrix and its note-on-evidence named
    SUPA-3/6 as Planned; leaving it untouched would re-introduce the
    contradiction this row removes.
    
    Addresses README-12.
    
